  "interpretation": "Document loss split into its four channels, and a counterfactual in which each system's grounding deficit is removed outright. structural_failure and grounding_failure are forced to loss 1.0; valid_empty is scored normally and is not forced (empty prediction against empty gold scores F1=1.0), it simply loses most of the time. Those three channels are where the Plan 2 grounding separation lives; valid_content_bearing is what the certificate actually measures. The grounding oracle measures coverage against the RESTRICTED population. That is NOT uniformly generous -- dropping a low-loss member raises a group's mean loss, and groups_worsened_by_restriction counts the cases -- so the conclusion does not rest on it. It rests on mean_loss_ceiling: a population whose mean loss exceeds alpha*c + (1-c) cannot reach coverage c at risk alpha under ANY selection rule. Where excluded_by_ceiling is true, arithmetic alone forbids the floor. Where it is false the ceiling is silent and the measured curve decides. Conditional coverage is not a deployable acceptance rate and is not comparable across systems. Nothing here selects a threshold or certifies anything.",
